Beringia is made of parts under different licenses, kept apart along the line between the Linux kernel and XNU.
Each source file names its license in an SPDX-License-Identifier line; the full texts are in LICENSES/:

  GPL-2.0-only   host/, scripts/, tools/, tests/, docs/
  APSL-2.0       loader/, xnu/patches/, kexts/
  MIT            host/include/beringia/host.h and xnu/include/beringia/*.h (interfaces shared by both sides)

Files without a comment syntax (patches, JSON, property lists) are under the license of the directory they are in.
Patches to XNU are modifications of Apple's APSL-2.0 code and are distributed under APSL-2.0.

Copyright (c) 2026 Beringia contributors.
